":"Public domain","licenseUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LE_Capsule.JPG","sourcePage":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LE_Capsule.JPG","sourceSha1":"a82581053b1e5cde464dd8eaa3a7565d3f621abd","use":"visual-reference-only","view":"Individually inspected north-bank exterior,00776p wider opposite view and LE Capsule close-up. Single-sided A-frame, two tension-spoke planes, white triangular rim truss, upright elliptical pods, transverse hoops and exterior radial mounts identified. Canonical32-pod configuration; no claim about temporary pod refurbishment status. Photographs are visual references only."},{"title":"File:London Eye (00776p).jpg","author":"Rhododendrites","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","sourcePage":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:London_Eye_(00776p).jpg","sourceSha1":"2e02d250a8f7712514344bb8bd8d7f982f4ba411","use":"visual-reference-only","view":"Individually inspected north-bank exterior,00776p wider opposite view and LE Capsule close-up. Single-sided A-frame, two tension-spoke planes, white triangular rim truss, upright elliptical pods, transverse hoops and exterior radial mounts identified. Canonical32-pod configuration; no claim about temporary pod refurbishment status. Photographs are visual references only."},{"title":"File:London Eye seen from the north bank of the Thames, London.jpg","author":"Christian David","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","sourcePage":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:London_Eye_seen_from_the_north_bank_of_the_Thames,_London.jpg","sourceSha1":"21fa7091c036c734f6ac9fd88da72278e692e9a9","use":"visual-reference-only","view":"Individually inspected north-bank exterior,00776p wider opposite view and LE Capsule close-up. Single-sided A-frame, two tension-spoke planes, white triangular rim truss, upright elliptical pods, transverse hoops and exterior radial mounts identified. Canonical32-pod configuration; no claim about temporary pod refurbishment status. Photographs are visual references only."}],"kind":"observation-wheel","aliases":["Millennium Wheel","London"],"authors":["Open Landmarks contributors"],"artisticLicense":"CC-BY-4.0","spatialDataLicense":"ODbL-1.0","licenseScope":"CC BY applies to original artistic contributions only; ODbL applies to OSM-derived spatial data. Reference photographs retain their own licenses. Dimension evidence from https://www.londoneye.com/about-us/history/, https://www.londoneye.com/plan-your-visit/information-and-support/faqs/ retains factual measurements; source documents are linked, not redistributed.","assistance":"AI-assisted architectural interpretation and procedural recipe authoring; deterministic Python/Blender export. No photographic textures.","review":{"status":"pending","reviewer":null,"checks":{},"notes":"Automated export and source-registration checks, and multi-view studio inspection, are retained in the linked evidence. Independent rights, appearance and map integration approval remains pending.","evidence":"https://github.com/benjamintd/open-landmarks/blob/main/collection/london-eye/review-evidence.json"},"modelingNotes":["Actual OSM way/204068874 (Q160659) supplies the wheel plane and anchor. The preserved446-part OSM authoring group supplies32 glass capsule positions and vertical intervals, rim slices, two one-sided support legs and boarding pavilion. Model envelope includes those mapped parts outside the narrow original wheel outline; it is not a filled building slab.","London Eye operator publishes135m height,120m wheel diameter and32 pods, and describes a single-sided cantilever with tension spokes and two angled legs. https://www.londoneye.com/about-us/history/ https://www.londoneye.com/plan-your-visit/information-and-support/faqs/ https://www.londoneye.com/our-company/blog/how-the-london-eye-was-built/ Source tags136.5m overall are retained unchanged; mapped vertical dimensions are scaled135/136.5 for the published height. Capsule frame at the highest mapped pod completes the135m tip.","Individually inspected Commons north-bank exterior and capsule close-up establish the triangular white rim truss, paired cable spoke planes, one-sided axle support, oval level capsules with transverse frame hoops, paired outside capsule cradles and low boarding canopy. Canonical32-pod configuration is modeled; the operator FAQ notes a temporarily removed pod for refurbishment, so this is not a claim about the operating fleet on a particular day.","Inference: rim chord radii60 and58.6m, tube radii.18-.34m, wire radius.065m, hub shoulder profile, capsule ellipsoid and hoop thickness, and omitted concealed portions of the23m spindle. The two support axes are fitted between mapped base slices and the axle; their source positions are retained. Tube sections and low-LOD wires are enlarged slightly for map readability.","Both authored LODs retain32 level pods, full open wheel, two spoke planes, triangular rim, cantilever legs and boarding platform. Low reduces curved sections and capsule hoops. Glazing is opaque libraryglass without photographic textures; seats, passengers, signs, branding, river water and interior machinery are omitted."],"source":{"url":"/objects/6ba173ef3a84776a82df98568e2592e528120367f819bb1f53faf3462eb016a7/source.blend.gz","bytes":810143,"sha256":"6ba173ef3a84776a82df98568e2592e528120367f819bb1f53faf3462eb016a7"},"spatialSource":{"url":"/objects/a839165b11f63c15d4ad101281e4fbfde794bf43506185356fc5c3191597b9d1/spatial-source.json","bytes":259457,"sha256":"a839165b11f63c15d4ad101281e4fbfde794bf43506185356fc5c3191597b9d1"},"preview":{"url":"/objects/e00026ec61e7285440156ffcd4b966a331742d7f78db390d1d5cb97478243920/preview.webp","bytes":37606,"sha256":"e00026ec61e7285440156ffcd4b966a331742d7f78db390d1d5cb97478243920"},"previewDirection":[-2,0.7,-0.1],"wikidata":"Q160659","revision":"630cc43535a4d4086917c767925405d11b8682f94f285367139c9f1404d8fe81","publication